            <ArticleTitle>Five men with chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The above ECGs represent typical findings in patients with chest pain. I hope that most GPs will have scored 100 per cent--but never forget that it is the patient's history and physical examination that really matters, not the ECG. All the information needed to interpret theses traces is included in 'The ECG Made Easy', 5th edition, written by the author and published by Churchill Livingstone. If you want some more practice at ECG interpretation, try '100 ECG Problems', also by the author and published by Churchill Livingstone.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
